{"name":"Adobe Village","hex":"#d6ae9a","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adobe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unburnt brick dried in the sun.","The earth from which such bricks are made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adobe"},{"term":"village","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rural habitation of size between a hamlet and a town.","A rural habitation that has a church, but no market."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/village"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adobe","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe is a building material made from loam and organic materials. Adobe is Spanish for mudbrick. In some English-speaking regions of Spanish heritage, such as the Southwestern United States, the term is used to refer to any kind of earthen construction, or various architectural styles like Pueblo Revival or Territorial Revival. Most adobe buildings are similar in appearance to cob and rammed earth buildings. Adobe is among the earliest building materials, and is used throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/330px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe","wikidata":"Q183496"},{"title":"Village","blocks":[{"text":"A village is a human settlement or a residential community, larger than a hamlet but smaller than a town; some geographers describe villages as having between 500 and 2,500 inhabitants. Although villages are often located in rural areas, the term urban village is also applied to certain urban neighborhoods. Villages are normally permanent, with fixed dwellings, however, transient villages also exist. Further, the dwellings of a village are fairly close to one another, not scattered broadly over the landscape, as a dispersed settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG/330px-Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Village","wikidata":"Q532"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/500px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/1280px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/500px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adobe wall (detail) in Bahillo, Palencia, Spain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdobe_wall_(detail)_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Renewal of the surface coating of an adobe wall in Chamisal, New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/1280px-Qasroddasht.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Qasroddasht.JPG/500px-Qasroddasht.JPG?u